  "text": "Where do MCP servers actually run? Depending on where your data lives, MCP supports two main transports. When connecting to local folders, personal notes, Git repositories, or a local database on your machine, the host launches the server as a tiny local subprocess using standard input and output—fast and completely private by default.",
